  "necessary_distinctions": [
    "Handler._handle_status -> RuntimeStatusView.block -> fetch -> RuntimeClient.status uses native runtime RPC once per reached HTTP handler, not a status-result cache.",
    "Host internal STATUS_RPC_TIMEOUT is750ms; external500ms timeout does not cancel/join that server handler. RuntimeClient.status_within has an existing native total_s boundary for the direct measurement client only.",
    "RuntimeClient._connect can create multiple sockets on backlog EAGAIN under bounded backoff. RPC calls are not socket-attempt or native DB-connection counts.",
    "Background importer worker None/exit and _ensure_worker allow later incarnations. _threads is a registry/prune, not a total lifetime cap.",
    "Background normal backoff updates after successful validation. Urgency bypasses normal deadlines; direct import_if_changed has its own admission and db.retry_locked.10s alone is not a bound for all entrypoints/failures.",
    "Seed startup invariants install native builtin Janitors in addition to three corpus owners. Actual setup raw state/scheduler controls are still needed; do not invent a three-agent total.",
    "Bookkeeping launch is conditional on active delegation rows. Cache warm-up has native provider capability discovery. Private raw-state and guard eligibility must be proved without disabling workers or expanding process/network authority."
  ]
